169
00:06:13,450 --> 00:06:15,415
That is their claim, not an established

170
00:06:15,435 --> 00:06:15,822
finding.

171
00:06:16,742 --> 00:06:18,719
Olson's death did not end the testing.

172
00:06:19,339 --> 00:06:21,929
In 1963, the Inspector General learned of

173
00:06:21,949 --> 00:06:24,602
the unwitting tests during a survey of the

174
00:06:24,622 --> 00:06:25,812
technical division.

175
00:06:26,282 --> 00:06:28,488
In May, the head of the covert operations

176
00:06:28,508 --> 00:06:30,660
directorate, by then Richard Helms, told

177
00:06:30,680 --> 00:06:32,398
him he had briefed the Director.

178
00:06:32,738 --> 00:06:35,023
According to the Inspector General, Helms

179
00:06:35,043 --> 00:06:36,710
said the Director indicated no

180
00:06:36,730 --> 00:06:38,904
disagreement, and therefore the testing

181
00:06:38,924 --> 00:06:39,691
will continue.

182
00:06:40,261 --> 00:06:42,505
The Inspector General recommended ending

183
00:06:42,525 --> 00:06:42,675
it.

184
00:06:43,015 --> 00:06:45,029
Following his report, the project was

185
00:06:45,049 --> 00:06:45,579
